   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-04-25">4. 25. 1942</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__313" type="person">Mr. H. Budzislawski</rs><lb/> c/o <rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__1915" type="person">Mrs. Dorothy Thompson</rs>.<lb/> 237
               East 48 Str.<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs><lb/>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__313" type="person">Mr.
                  Budzislawski</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>You will get once more next week a speech from myself. During the week after May 4th.
            I am as I have told you already on a lecturing trip and unable to deliver a speech. This means
            that I have to ask somebody else and that the matter I referred in my last letter must be decided
            in the meantime. Please, let me know as soon as possible how the situation is.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Cordially yours</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Paul
                  Tillich</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
